window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><i>The Lost Heir</i></p> <p>He’s lost everything. Even his memory. Nothing remains. Now she is all grown up, Miss Elizabeth Bennet’s heart whispers all sorts of possibilities for the grave, well-mannered—and handsome—mysterious man. While he struggles to come to terms with his true identity, can Fitzwilliam Darcy keep his beloved—and his new-found family—safe?</p> <p><i>Imagining Mr. Darcy</i></p> <p>Darcy doesn't like young ladies who unsettle his inner equilibrium, whose impertinent comments offend the inborn pride of his position. Elizabeth Bennet doesn't like proud, arrogant gentlemen, who make disparaging comments about her and her family. Each has to imagine what the other is really like. But how can they really know? And which one do they really love?</p> <p><i>The Wrong Brother</i></p> <p>Fitzwilliam Darcy has lost his birthright. When his malign elder brother arrives uninvited at Netherfield, George decides to steal Elizabeth Bennet’s heart. The heir to Pemberley is the son-in-law of Mrs. Bennet's dreams. But Elizabeth favours the younger brother. Mama is vexed. Surely, Fitzwilliam Darcy is an impossible union. She cannot permit it. Will Elizabeth be proved right to have favoured the wrong brother?</p> <p><i>Married for Revenge</i></p> <p>Elizabeth Bennet will never forgive Mr. Darcy. Never. And now he has compounded his sins by forcing her to marry him—for revenge. Every man has his price—and it has cost Darcy a fortune. But he must take the chance to marry Miss Elizabeth Bennet. Battered by the need to forgive, the need to earn love, and the struggle to save Pemberley before it is too late—how will the two ever win their happy ever after?</p> <p><i>Her Very Own Mr. Darcy</i></p> <p>Neither Darcy nor Elizabeth believe in love at first sight. Elizabeth’s sorrow for the long-dead Flora from an old diary complicates her decision whether to accept this Mr. Darcy—and all his many troubles</p>"; 
